1302 0 obj
<<
/Title (From a clinical perspective, a chronic condition like diabetes does not act as a seasonal flu; it cannot realistically experience such a massive, sudden drop overnight. Therefore, this drastic variation strongly points toward data collection artifacts, changes in diagnostic coding/classification, or categorization shifts across years rather than a real-world shift in patient demographics. This highlights the need for standardized data entry and consistent disease coding protocols in future data tracking)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1299 0 R
/First 1305 0 R
/Last 1306 0 R
/Count -3
>>
